French science guys.

00:07:14.977 --> 00:07:17.347
"We should measure this
distance right here,

00:07:17.347 --> 00:07:19.117
"and divide it by ten a bunch of times,

00:07:19.117 --> 00:07:21.787
"and get a really precise unit of measure

00:07:21.787 --> 00:07:24.390
"so that we don't have to
use our feet and arms."

00:07:24.390 --> 00:07:25.440
Great idea!

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:26.460
But how the hell do you get

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:29.340
this massive measurement in 1792?

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:33.210
And the answer was this
thing, plus some math.

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:34.770
So these two French astronomers

00:07:34.770 --> 00:07:36.180
go out into the French countryside,

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:40.950
looking for high up places
like hills or castle towers.

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:43.890
And then, they look
through this fancy little

00:07:43.890 --> 00:07:46.410
platinum map telescope and measure

00:07:46.410 --> 00:07:49.800
the angles between two
points out in the distance.

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:52.590
This fancy telescope allows
them to make this measurement

00:07:52.590 --> 00:07:55.200
without having to walk
these whole distances.

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:57.210
And in this way, they could start making

00:07:57.210 --> 00:08:00.030
little triangles across
the French countryside.

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:01.770
And then, using some basic math

00:08:01.770 --> 00:08:03.450
that we all learned in middle school,

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:07.230
they could start to calculate
a hyper-accurate distance

00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:09.120
along this straight line.

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:13.290
It took them seven years
to calculate all of this,

00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:14.133
but they got it!

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:17.310
And once they had this distance,

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:19.470
they were able to calculate this distance:

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:21.060
between the north pole and the equator,

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:23.070
one-fourth of the earth's circumference.

00:08:23.070 --> 00:08:25.470
So they took this line, this measurement,

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:28.560
and they chopped it up into
10 million little parts

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:32.250
and one of those parts
is called a 'meter'.

00:08:32.250 --> 00:08:36.510
Like, this is pegged to a
real unchanging measurement

00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:38.070
that is our Earth!

00:08:38.070 --> 00:08:40.486
I mean, it'll change eventually.

00:08:40.486 --> 00:08:41.319
(explosion)

00:08:41.319 --> 00:08:42.180
But not in our lifetimes.

00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:44.310
The name meter comes from
the Greek word "metron,"

00:08:44.310 --> 00:08:45.690
which means "a measurement,"

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:48.120
which is just super literal and precise

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:50.550
and exactly what the French
Enlightenment was all about.

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:53.130
- [Announcer] Now, here's
what it's all about.

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:53.963
The meter.

00:08:53.963 --> 00:08:55.140
- So now you have this meter,

00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:57.570
and if you divide this into
a hundred smaller units,

00:08:57.570 --> 00:08:59.490
you have a centimeter.

00:08:59.490 --> 00:09:00.750
Centimeter.

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:03.000
So put a thousand of these side by side,

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:05.670
and you get yourself a kilometer.

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:06.510
A kilometer.

00:09:06.510 --> 00:09:08.310
- The best part about the metric system

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:10.410
is the time it saves in computation.

00:09:10.410 --> 00:09:11.490
- Wait a minute. I can do this.

00:09:11.490 --> 00:09:12.330
It's all about tens.

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:15.750
So if this measurement
was ten million of these,

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:19.172
divide that by a thousand, you
get ten thousand kilometers.

00:09:19.172 --> 00:09:20.005
(upbeat trumpet music)

00:09:20.005 --> 00:09:21.002
Okay, so this is ten thousand kilometers.

00:09:21.002 --> 00:09:22.050
(upbeat trumpet music)

00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:23.927
One-fourth of the earth's circumference.

00:09:23.927 --> 00:09:25.050
(upbeat trumpet music)

00:09:25.050 --> 00:09:26.224
Four of these should be...

00:09:26.224 --> 00:09:27.240
(upbeat trumpet music)

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:28.972
Forty thousand kilometers!

00:09:28.972 --> 00:09:29.880
(upbeat music)

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:32.230
The earth's circumference
is 40,000 kilometers!

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:35.550
Wait, what? No, I don't want miles.

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:37.950
Come on, what? It should be 40,000.

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:40.440
What's this extra 75
kilometers doing here?

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:42.720
Well, it turns out that one
of these French astronomers

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:45.390
